    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with significant firepower, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.92) and **Trea Turner** (79.76). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier play, leveraging a prime lead-off spot against Warren with a +14% boost from favorable platoon dynamics. Similarly, **Trea Turner** remains an elite anchor; his high speed profile is critical for our stolen base objectives, and he enjoys a +16% park factor boost that helps maximize his efficiency against Young. **Kyle Schwarber** (78.41) and **Junior Caminero** (76.86) also sit in our elite tier, with **Kyle Schwarber** benefiting from a massive park adjustment and **Junior Caminero** showing strong xWOBA metrics (0.370) against a vulnerable Fedde. We are leaning heavily into the platoon edges offered by these matchups to outpace the field.\n\nThe toughest decision on the bench involved **Lars Nootbaar** (47.14), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While **Lars Nootbaar** posted a respectable score bolstered by a +11% dynamic platoon edge, his matchup against a high-tier arm like Cease (2.94 xERA) suppressed his upside compared to the rest of the outfield. We opted to prioritize the higher raw efficiency of **Carson Benge** and the elite power profile of **Yordan Alvarez**, even though **Yordan Alvarez** faces a tougher test against Eovaldi. Elsewhere, we continue to monitor the status of **Hyeseong Kim** and **Nelson Velazquez**, who remain inactive, while ensuring we stay above our 40.0 floor with hitters like **Chase Meidroth** (49.27) to preserve our precious game caps. We enter this evening with high confidence, though we remain vigilant regarding the heavy workload placed on our core speed threats in the 5x5 categories.",
